    {
      "id": "p0088-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "There are multiple words that can mean \"determination\" in Japanese, but none contain the multiple meanings behind Undertale's \"determination\". For the localization team, this meant that certain things would be lost in translation no matter what. The term still needed to be translated into something, though, so after some discussion, the team settled on the word ketsui (\"determination; resolve; decisiveness; a made-up mind\") for Undertale's \"determination\".",
        "raw": "There are multiple words that can mean \"determination\" in Japanese, but none\ncontain the multiple meanings behind Underta/e's \"determination\". For the\nlocalization team, this meant that certain things would be lost in translation\nno matter what. The term still needed to be translated into something, though,\nso after some discussion, the team settled on the word ketsui (\"determination;\nresolve; decisiveness; a made-up mind\") for Underta/e's \"determination\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29120158,
          0.32963571,
          0.90154869,
          0.43341429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28736234,
          0.32892143,
          0.9055916,
          0.43448571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25,
          26
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日语中有几个词都能表示 determination，但没有哪个词能涵盖 Undertale 赋予它的多重含义。这意味着，本地化团队无论如何都会在翻译中有所损失。可它终究得有个译法。经过讨论，团队选定了 ketsui，意思包括“决心、决意、果断、打定主意”，用来对应 Undertale 中的 determination。",
        "status": "draft",
